From 40ff9edddd97057fb304281297cade5c41e1b41e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:59:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(lifecycle): preserve reaching stdin provenance [daveey]

Replace command-wide assignment/fd unions with a deliberately narrow flat-sequence
proof. Future, conditional, function-local and subshell definitions cannot erase
inherited or unknown stdin. Freeze expansions at assignment/redirection time;
resolve descriptors left-to-right and persist only standalone exec definitions.
Unknown mutations invalidate subsequent variable proofs, including nameref and
readonly attributes; quoted assignment words are not proven assignments. Export
arguments expand against their pre-command snapshot, unlike assignment-only words.

PR3099 rework: variable scope/order and descriptor scope/order were lost when
segment-view unions replaced the inherited source without a reaching definition.
This patch preserves uncertainty instead of claiming that any syntactic definition
is necessarily in force. Unsupported compound flow may refuse earlier with a
cannot-resolve reason; nine existing cases now assert that exact reason rather
than SQLite after guessing a file. No piped-file behavior is changed.

TDD: variable RED 10 cases, fd RED 9 cases incl closed-fd control, nameref RED 2,
quoted/declaration RED 4 plus duplicate assignment RED 1. Focused GREEN 391 tests
including harmless real-Bash marker oracles. Scoped scripts/check:20 checks OK.
Full --base origin/main gate is not green: stale stacked base has unrelated
agent_runtime_helpers FILE_LINES and process_registry NESTING failures. Must rebase
only after parent PR3039/2911 land, rerun full gates, independent exact-head review
and required CI before canonical hermes-core-wt ship. No merge authorization here.
